\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Short-Circuit Evaluation with AndAlso\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab When using the And operator, if the first expression is false, then the entire expression will be false\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab If there is no need to evaluate the second expression, it can be skipped using a method called short-circuit evaluation\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab In Visual Basic you use the AndAlso operator to achieve short-circuit evaluation\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 25\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Short-Circuit Evaluation with AndAlso (cont.)\b0\par
