\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Precedence of Logical Operators\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Logical operators have an order of precedence just as arithmetic operators do\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf5 From}{\cf5  }{\cf5 highest}{\cf5  }{\cf2 to}{\cf5  }{\cf5 lowest}{\cf5  }{\cf5 precedence}\line {\cf2 Not}\line {\cf2 And}\line {\cf2 Or}\line {\cf2 Xor}\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab As with arithmetic operations, parentheses are often used to clarify order of operations\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 32\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Precedence of Logical Operators\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab For example, in the statement\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf2 If}{\cf5  }{\cf5 x}{\cf5  }{\cf5 <}{\cf5  }{\cf6 0}{\cf5  }{\cf2 And}{\cf5  }{\cf5 y}{\cf5  }{\cf5 >}{\cf5  }{\cf6 100}{\cf5  }{\cf2 Or}{\cf5  }{\cf5 z}{\cf5  }{\cf5 =}{\cf5  }{\cf6 50}\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab x < 0 And y > 100 is evaluated first\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab If the And condition is true, we then evaluate\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf2 True}{\cf5  }{\cf2 Or}{\cf5  }{\cf5 z}{\cf5  }{\cf5 =}{\cf5  }{\cf6 50}\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab If the And condition is false, we then evaluate\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf2 False}{\cf5  }{\cf2 Or}{\cf5  }{\cf5 z}{\cf5  }{\cf5 =}{\cf5  }{\cf6 50}\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab If the Or condition is to be evaluated first, parentheses must be used\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf2 If}{\cf5  }{\cf5 x}{\cf5  }{\cf5 <}{\cf5  }{\cf6 0}{\cf5  }{\cf2 And}{\cf5  }{\cf5 (}{\cf5 y}{\cf5  }{\cf5 >}{\cf5  }{\cf6 100}{\cf5  }{\cf2 Or}{\cf5  }{\cf5 z}{\cf5  }{\cf5 =}{\cf5  }{\cf6 50}{\cf5 )}\par
\pard\sb520\sa40\keepn\f0\fs18\cf5 SLIDE 33\par
\pard\sa120\keepn\b\fs34\cf2 Math, Relational, &  Logical Operators\b0\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Evaluate the following if: a=5, b=7, x=100, y=30\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf2 If}{\cf5  }{\cf5 x}{\cf5  }{\cf5 >}{\cf5  }{\cf5 a}{\cf5  }{\cf5 *}{\cf5  }{\cf6 10}{\cf5  }{\cf2 And}{\cf5  }{\cf5 y}{\cf5  }{\cf5 <}{\cf5  }{\cf5 b}{\cf5  }{\cf5 +}{\cf5  }{\cf6 20}\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab Evaluating the math operators leaves us with\par
\pard\li360\sb60\sa140\f1\fs22\cf5 {\cf2 If}{\cf5  }{\cf5 x}{\cf5  }{\cf5 >}{\cf5  }{\cf6 50}{\cf5  }{\cf2 And}{\cf5  }{\cf5 y}{\cf5  }{\cf5 <}{\cf5  }{\cf6 27}\line {\cf5 Evaluating}{\cf5  }{\cf5 the}{\cf5  }{\cf5 relational}{\cf5  }{\cf5 operators}{\cf5  }{\cf5 leaves}\par
