\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab A nested loop is a loop inside another loop\par
\pard\tx360\li360\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8226?\tab The hands of a clock make a good example\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab The hour hand makes 1 revolution for every 60 revolutions of the minute hand\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab The minute hand makes 1 revolution for every 60 revolutions of the second hand\par
\pard\tx720\li720\fi-360\sa80\f0\fs26\cf1 \u8211?\tab For every revolution of the hour hand the second hand makes 36,000 revolutions\par
